at is needed to address diagnostics."}, {"id": "f7996ba4-f2f9-4e8a-86ee-b9bc3e39316c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diagnostics", "children": [], "description": "Diagnostics makes the validity limits of linear-model synthesis explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. After normal theory, diagnostics supplies what is needed to address model misspecification."}, {"id": "1712f06c-bca2-4520-8aea-8478ffb87cd5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Model misspecification", "children": [], "description": "Model misspecification gives linear-model synthesis a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final course topic, model misspecification requires ideas from the complete path to be integrated and transferred."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$mathstatzzjs$::jsonb,
